course: dictionary
lesson: 10899
title: One word, two worlds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Never touch a bat; some bats carry rabies or similar viruses.» Here a virus is a tiny living thing that can make animals ill.
explain: The same word can also belong to computers. «A girl downloaded a cheat that put a virus on the family computer.» Ask yourself: is this sentence about being ill, or about a computer? The clues tell you which.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. A germ fits with «ill» and «spread», while a harmful program fits with «computer» and «account». If your meaning makes sense, you have it.
fact: A virus is a tiny germ, much too small to see, that gets inside living cells.
fact: Viruses can make people, animals or plants ill, for example with colds, flu, chickenpox and measles.
fact: «Most viruses are much smaller than bacteria and too small to be seen with an ordinary light microscope.»
fact: Antibiotics do not kill viruses, but vaccines can protect against some of them.
fact: A computer virus is a harmful program that spreads between computers and can damage them or steal information.
exercise: «Some bats carry rabies or similar viruses.» What is a virus in this sentence? | A large animal that lives in caves | A cheat for an online game | *A tiny germ that can make animals ill | A type of computer screen
exercise: «It put a virus on the family computer and her account was banned.» What does virus mean here? | A fast game on a phone | *A harmful program that damages computers | A kind of bat | A tiny germ that makes people sneeze
exercise: Which illness is caused by a virus? | A sprained ankle | *Chickenpox | Sunburn | A broken arm
test: Which action helps protect a computer from a virus? | Sharing your password with a stranger | Opening every strange link you are sent | Turning the screen up as bright as it goes | *Using antivirus software and not opening strange attachments
test: Why does washing your hands help stop viruses spreading? | *Viruses can spread on dirty hands, so clean hands help | Antibiotics are hidden in water | Hands make viruses grow bigger | Viruses are attracted to soap
exam: Which statement about viruses and antibiotics is true? | Viruses are killed by sunshine every day | Antibiotics kill all viruses | Vaccines and antibiotics are the same thing | *Antibiotics do not kill viruses
